The earlier PR https://github.com/coax-dev/coax/pull/6 did not add the entropy regularization bonus to the q function targets. This PR fixes that and also changes the API of the `NStepEntropyRegularizer` to accept a collection of (time-) indices whose entropy should be discounted and added to the bonus.

So in the provided example, the q function targets get an entropy bonus of `\gamma^{5} * -\log \pi(s_{t + 5})` and the policy receives a bonus of `-\log \pi(s_{t}) + \gamma * -\log \pi(s_{t + 1}) + \gamma^{2} * -\log \pi(s_{t + 2}) + \gamma^{3} * -\log \pi(s_{t + 3}) + \gamma^{4} * -\log \pi(s_{t + 4})`.

@KristianHolsheimer If you are ok with this change I will add the appropriate documentation. But first I wanted to make sure that this is the way to go.

Hiya, this PR contains several minor fixes for the DiMUSE engine:

1. A fix for [this ](https://bugs.scummvm.org/ticket/13084) bug;
2. A fix for an issue in which streamZone aren't correctly deallocated when terminating the engine or releasing a dispatch;
3. A fix for both DiMUSE streams being kept busy after skipping a SMUSH video in DIG full version (I simply forgot to implement the correct behavior...);
